<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39391" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίηρα</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρειν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦρα φέρειν</span>
			 or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦρα ἐπιφέρειν</span>, bring
			one <i>acceptable</i>
			<i>gifts</i>, render <i>service</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίηρα φέροντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					1094
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Rhian.
				1.21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίηρα φέρεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.375
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέχθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					13.22
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Phaedim.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίηρα</span>, as
			Adv., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάριν</span>
			, <i>for the sake of</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antim.
				87
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃς κακὰ πόλλ᾽ ὑπέμεινε μιῆς</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. θυγατρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PHamb.</u>
					22.2
				</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. sg.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίηρος</span>
			<i>pleasant, grate ful</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					96.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simm.
					6.3
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιηρέστερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					186
				</span></i>
			. Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦρα,
		ἐπιήρανος</span>.</div>
